WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.848 --> 00:00:10.309
Priya Raman: Hi Megan, how are you doing today?

2
00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:14.162
Megan Foster: Hey Priya, I'm good. Busy week. How about you?

3
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:23.242
Priya Raman: Same here. I wanted to check in on how things are going with call tracking and Signal AI across the practices.

4
00:00:23.242 --> 00:00:24.467
Priya Raman: Anything standing out?

5
00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:37.483
Megan Foster: Mostly good. Call volumes look normal for October, maybe a little up with the fall promos. The practice managers are still opening their call summaries every morning, so that habit stuck.

6
00:00:38.127 --> 00:00:45.916
Priya Raman: That's what we like to hear. Any changes on your side staffing wise? I know you had someone out for a bit.

7
00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:55.318
Megan Foster: Yeah, one of our front desk leads at the Meridian office was out for two weeks, so the Boise team covered phones.

8
00:00:55.318 --> 00:00:57.727
Megan Foster: Things are back to normal now.

9
00:00:58.252 --> 00:01:03.312
Priya Raman: Good. And are you still running the new patient campaign through Google Ads?

10
00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:15.410
Megan Foster: We are, that's the main driver. Which is actually why I wanted to talk to you today. We've got an issue with the offline conversions going to Google Ads.

11
00:01:16.188 --> 00:01:18.657
Priya Raman: Okay, tell me what you're seeing.

12
00:01:19.607 --> 00:01:28.122
Megan Foster: So the call conversions are landing in Google Ads, but they show up one to three days after the call. Sometimes two days, sometimes three.

13
00:01:28.122 --> 00:01:29.144
Megan Foster: It's not consistent.

14
00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:33.507
Priya Raman: And that timing is a problem because?

15
00:01:33.995 --> 00:01:44.481
Megan Foster: Because Smart Bidding is making decisions on partial data. If it doesn't know about half the new patient calls for two days, it's optimizing on an incomplete picture.

16
00:01:44.481 --> 00:01:47.102
Megan Foster: We're spending real money on those campaigns.

17
00:01:48.286 --> 00:01:52.698
Priya Raman: That makes sense. Have you checked anything on your end?

18
00:01:53.849 --> 00:02:04.865
Megan Foster: We did. We went through the GCLID capture and the Invoca tag, everything looks right. Nothing changed on our side. I even had our web person double check the tag placement.

19
00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:06.642
Megan Foster: So we're kind of stuck.

20
00:02:06.856 --> 00:02:10.020
Priya Raman: Got it. Do you know when this started? Roughly?

21
00:02:10.384 --> 00:02:19.403
Megan Foster: Maybe three weeks ago. I noticed it when I was pulling the weekly report and the numbers looked thin, then caught up later.

22
00:02:20.745 --> 00:02:24.445
Priya Raman: Okay. Does it affect all campaigns or just certain ones?

23
00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:37.610
Megan Foster: As far as I can tell it's all of them, but I haven't looked at every single one. The new patient ones are the ones I watch closest.

24
00:02:38.156 --> 00:02:53.946
Priya Raman: Let me take this back to the team and find out what's going on with the delivery timing. I'll want to look at a couple of specific calls, so can you send me two or three examples with the call times?

25
00:02:55.189 --> 00:02:58.022
Megan Foster: Yes, I can pull those together this afternoon.

26
00:02:58.258 --> 00:03:03.910
Priya Raman: Perfect. In the meantime, everything else on the Signal AI side is fine?

27
00:03:04.448 --> 00:03:06.137
Megan Foster: Yeah, no complaints there.

28
00:03:07.549 --> 00:03:16.815
Priya Raman: Good. One more thing, we should set up a short call before your next quarterly review. Does the first week of November work?

29
00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:21.948
Megan Foster: Let's do the fourth if that works. I'll send an invite.

30
00:03:22.995 --> 00:03:29.481
Priya Raman: Sounds good. I'll follow up on the conversion timing as soon as I hear back. Talk soon.

31
00:03:30.884 --> 00:03:32.008
Megan Foster: Thanks, Priya. Bye.
